# Autonomy Daemon Core Development Rules

## CRITICAL: Never Simplify or Remove Functionality
- **NEVER simplify or remove functionality** - this makes the codebase harder to maintain and debug
- Missing functionality is extremely difficult to track down later
- Always fix the actual issue, not work around it
- Preserve all existing behavior and features

## LOGX Logging System
- **ALWAYS use LOGX macros** instead of printf for logging
- Use correct LOGX macro names: `LOGX_INFO_MSG`, `LOGX_ERROR_MSG`, `LOGX_WARN_MSG`, `LOGX_DEBUG_MSG`
- **NEVER use**: `LOGX_INFO`, `LOGX_ERROR`, `LOGX_WARN`, `LOGX_DEBUG` (these are incorrect)
- If LOGX calls are broken, fix them rather than replacing with printf
- Include proper error handling for all LOGX calls

## Build System Requirements
- **ALWAYS use the build script**: `/mnt/wsl/SDK/build_autonomy_daemon.sh`
- **NEVER run make commands manually** - this can cause caching issues
- The build script handles proper cache cleaning and SDK toolchain usage
- Always wait for build completion before analyzing results

## Version Management
- **ALWAYS update version files** when making changes:
  - `/mnt/s/autonomy/VERSION` (increment build number)
  - `/mnt/s/autonomy/src/c/autonomy-daemon/core/version.h` (update build number and version string)
  - `/mnt/s/autonomy/src/c/autonomy-daemon/ubus/ubus_methods.c` (update hardcoded version strings)
- Verify version before testing: `ssh -i ~/.ssh/rutos_key root@192.168.80.1 "LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/usr/lib:/usr/lib timeout 5 /usr/local/usr/bin/autonomy-daemon --version"`

## UCI API Usage
- **Use existing uci_manager functions** that use `ucix_*` wrapper functions
- **NEVER use raw UCI API** directly (uci_set, uci_lookup_ptr, etc.)
- Use wrapper functions: `ucix_get_option`, `ucix_add_option`, etc.
- Maintain all UCI operations intact, just use the correct API calls

## Error Handling and Compilation
- **Systematic error search**: When fixing compilation errors, always search for the same error pattern across the entire codebase
- Use `/mnt/wsl/SDK/compilation_error_detector.sh` for automated fixes
- **SAFE for automated fixes**: LOGX macro corrections, format specifiers, missing includes, Unicode character removal
- **REQUIRES MANUAL REVIEW**: Type definition conflicts, function signature changes, UCI API usage, variable name changes

## Code Quality Standards
- Use C99 standard with proper error handling
- Include proper header guards: `#ifndef HEADER_H` / `#define HEADER_H` / `#endif`
- Use consistent naming: snake_case for functions and variables, UPPER_CASE for constants
- Always check return values and handle errors appropriately
- Use proper memory management with malloc/free pairs

## Testing and Deployment
- **5-minute runtime test**: Always run comprehensive 5-minute test after deployment
- Use deployment script: `/mnt/wsl/SDK/deploy_autonomy_daemon.sh`
- Monitor with: `/mnt/wsl/SDK/check_build_status.sh`
- Check build log at: `/mnt/wsl/SDK/autonomy_build.log`

## Module Enablement Strategy
- **Enable one module at a time** - never enable multiple modules simultaneously
- Build and test after each enablement
- Fix conflicts immediately - if multiple definitions occur, disable the duplicate
- Prioritize full implementations over simple/stub versions